<FILENAME>ea020554601ex99-1_earlyworks.htm
<DESCRIPTION>EARLYWORKS ANNOUNCES PLAN TO IMPLEMENT ADS RATIO CHANGE
<TEXT>
<HTML>
<HEAD>
     <TITLE></TITLE>
</HEAD>
<BODY STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif">

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: right"><B>Exhibit 99.1</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: center"><B>Earlyworks&nbsp;Announces Plan to Implement
ADS Ratio Change</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">Tokyo,
Japan, May 13 2024 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Earlyworks Co., Ltd. (Nasdaq: ELWS) (the &ldquo;Company&rdquo; or &ldquo;Earlyworks&rdquo;), a
Japanese company operating its proprietary private blockchain technology, Grid Ledger System (&ldquo;GLS&rdquo;), announced plans to <FONT STYLE="background-color: white">change
the ratio of its American Depository Shares (&ldquo;ADSs&rdquo;) to its ordinary shares from one (1)&nbsp;ADS, representing one (1)&nbsp;ordinary
share, to one (1)&nbsp;ADS representing five (5)&nbsp;ordinary shares (the &ldquo;ADS Ratio&rdquo;). The change in the ADS Ratio is expected
to become effective on or about May 16</FONT></FONT><FONT STYLE="background-color: white">&#65292;<FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">2024
(the &ldquo;Effective Date&rdquo;).</FONT></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; background-color: white">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; background-color: white">For the Company&rsquo;s
ADS holders, the change in the ADS Ratio has the same effect as a&nbsp;one-for-five&nbsp;reverse ADS split and will have no impact on
an ADS holder&rsquo;s proportional equity interest in the Company. The change in the ADS Ratio is intended to further support the liquidity
in the Company&rsquo;s ADSs and to enable the Company to regain compliance with the Nasdaq minimum bid price requirement.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; background-color: white">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; background-color: white">On the Effective Date,
registered holders of the Company&rsquo;s ADSs held in certificated form will be required on a mandatory basis to surrender their certificated
ADSs to Bank of New York Mellon, the depositary bank (the &ldquo;Depositary&rdquo;), for cancellation and will receive one (1)&nbsp;new
ADS in exchange for every five (5)&nbsp;existing ADSs surrendered. Holders of uncertificated ADSs in the Direct Registration System (DRS)
and The Depository Trust Company (DTC) will have their ADSs automatically exchanged and need not take any action.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; background-color: white">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; background-color: white">The exchange of every
five (5)&nbsp;then-held (existing) ADSs for one (1)&nbsp;new ADS will occur automatically at the Effective Date, with the then-held ADSs
being cancelled and new ADSs being issued by the Depositary. The Company&rsquo;s ADSs will continue to be traded on The Nasdaq Capital
Market under the ticker symbol &ldquo;ELWS.&rdquo;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; background-color: white">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; background-color: white">No fractional new ADSs
will be issued in connection with the change in the ADS Ratio. Instead, fractional entitlements to new ADSs will be aggregated and sold,
and the net cash proceeds from the sale of the fractional ADS entitlements (after deduction of fees, taxes, and expenses) will be distributed
to the applicable ADS holders by the Depositary.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; background-color: white">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; background-color: white">As a result of the change
in the ADS Ratio, the ADS trading price is expected to increase proportionally, although the Company can give no assurance that the ADS
trading price after the change in the ADS Ratio will be proportionally equal to or greater than the previous ADS trading price prior to
the change or that the change in the ADS Ratio will have any effect on the liquidity in the Company&rsquo;s ADSs.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; background-color: white">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: center; background-color: white"><B>Earlyworks appealed
the Nasdaq Delisting Determination</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">As previously disclosed in the Company&rsquo;s press release dated May 6, 2024, the Company received a staff determination letter, on
May 1, 2024, from the Listing Qualifications Department of The Nasdaq Stock Market LLC (&ldquo;Nasdaq&rdquo;) notifying the Company that,
due to the Company&rsquo;s failure to regain compliance with a minimum bid price of $1.00 per share requirement for continued listing
on The Nasdaq Capital Market, as set forth in Nasdaq Listing Rule 5550(a)(2), Nasdaq has determined (the &ldquo;Determination&rdquo;)
that Company&rsquo;s securities will be scheduled for delisting from Nasdaq unless the Company requests an appeal of the Determination
to a Hearings Panel (the &ldquo;Panel&rdquo;). On May 7, 2024, the Company appealed the delisting determination and requested a hearing
before the Panel. Such a request automatically stays any suspension or delisting action pending a final written decision by the Panel.
On May 7, 2024, the Company was notified that the hearing before the Panel has been scheduled on June 18, 2024.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>About Earlyworks Co., Ltd.</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">Earlyworks Co., Ltd. is a Japanese company operating
its proprietary private blockchain technology, GLS, to leverage blockchain technology in various applications in a wide range of industries.
GLS is a hybrid blockchain that combines the technical advantages of blockchain and database technology. GLS features high-speed processing,
which can reach 0.016 seconds per transaction, tamper-resistance, security, zero server downtime, and versatile applications. The applicability
of GLS is verified in multiple domains, including real estate, advertisement, telecommunications, metaverse, and financial services. The
Company&rsquo;s mission is to keep updating GLS and make it an infrastructure in the coming Web3/metaverse-like data society.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"></P>

